\subsection{Odd chains and the Sultanov Silence}

Marat Sultanov applied TAT-7 triadic resonance analysis to odd-numbered chains ($N=3,5,7,\dots,21$) with the contradiction edge placed at the center bond. No statistically significant triadic resonance was found for any odd $N$ in the standard gap$\times$fine triad. This is in stark contrast to even chains ($N=4,6,\dots,20$), where all cases show robust resonance ($p \leq 0.026$, agreement $>0.97$). The parity separation is perfect---no even chain fails, no odd chain passes. This decisively rules out divisibility by 3 as a confound, as $N=4,8,10,14,16,20$ are all even but not divisible by 3, yet all resonate.

Sultanov's discovery is thus generalized from the ``prime-chain silence'' to the \textbf{Sultanov Silence}: the complete absence of triadic resonance in symmetric odd chains, which marks a fundamental boundary condition for Silent Discordance. Notably, at $N=19$, a resonance with $p=0.02$ appears in the coarse$\times$gradient(fine) triad, suggesting that the structure does not vanish for large odd chains but migrates to a different diagnostic channel. This remains an open observation.

\subsection{Summary of the extended laws}

Based on the SOC, cyclic driving, non-equilibrium, current algebra, and odd-chain experiments, the behavior of Silent Discordance is governed by six laws. The first three govern the necessary and sufficient conditions for its emergence; the latter three govern its behavior in dynamic and rule-extension dimensions:

\textbf{First law: law of cycle necessity.} (Unchanged) \\
\textbf{Second law: law of fully symmetric interaction necessity.} (Unchanged) \\
\textbf{Third law: law of morphology-structure correspondence.} (Unchanged, but extended to include parity and asymmetry conditions) \\
\textbf{Fourth law: law of spin-flip channel sufficiency.} Silent Discordance survives under Rashba SOC as long as the interaction retains sufficient spin-flip channels. SOC does not act as a simple tuning knob, and its effect is most pronounced at the valley. \\
\textbf{Fifth law: law of Markovianity at small scales.} The relational field exhibits no memory effects under cyclic driving. \\
\textbf{Sixth law: law of asymmetric driving necessity.} Silent Discordance requires asymmetric injection of contradiction to trigger abrupt reorganization. Symmetric driving leads to smooth adaptation and no valley. This unifies the shift experiments, the current algebra model, and the non-equilibrium results.

\section{Discussion}

\subsection{Relation to known physics}

The three necessary and sufficient conditions of Silent Discordance have no systematic counterpart in known physics. It is not a quantum phase transition (the energy gap may not close), not an abrupt change of entanglement entropy (the diagnosis uses standard deviation and tail slope), and not a simple analogue of the Edwards--Anderson spin-glass order parameter~\cite{EdwardsAnderson1975}---Silent Discordance diagnoses the non-monotonic reorganization process of the relational field, rather than the static order of a frozen disordered state.

The relationship between Silent Discordance and known physics can be examined from two methodological perspectives. From an entity-first viewpoint, it may appear as a modest numerical observation in small lattice models, whose thermodynamic stability remains to be established. From a relation-first viewpoint, it is a universal dynamical signature of relational-field reorganization driven by contradiction, independent of entity diagnostics, with its morphology jointly determined by graph topology and the symmetry of contradiction injection. These two perspectives are not mutually exclusive---they are different interpretative frameworks for the same set of data. The present study adopts the latter, because it not only accounts for the observed morphological diversity, but has also successfully predicted the absence of triadic resonance on odd-numbered chains (the Sultanov Silence), the critical effect of contradiction-edge position, and the exact identity under bond-scaled $D/J$ uniformity---predictions that would not naturally arise within an entity-first framework. We invite the reader to judge, after examining the data, which framework offers greater explanatory and predictive power.

\subsection{Symmetry-breaking-driven relational reorganization}

A unifying theme emerges from the shift experiments, the current algebra model, and the non-equilibrium steady-state verification: \textbf{Silent Discordance is triggered by asymmetric contradiction injection.} Symmetric driving (uniform Zeeman field, central defect on prime chains, equilibrium cyclic driving) leads to smooth adaptation of the relational field without abrupt reorganization. Asymmetric driving (off-center defect, left-right Zeeman bias, non-equilibrium spin bias) forces the relational field to undergo a sudden, global, non-monotonic reorganization. This constitutes the core of a potential seventh law: the necessity of symmetry breaking in the driving field.

